WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.307
You are reviewing the fictional V two zero
one handover.

2
00:00:03.457 --> 00:00:07.958
The intended use is documented and the
material records are available.

3
00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:12.012
However, the required mixing range has not
been finalized,

4
00:00:12.162 --> 00:00:16.749
the transfer-hose cleaning evidence is
missing and the alarm response has

5
00:00:16.899 --> 00:00:18.221
not been verified.

6
00:00:18.371 --> 00:00:20.640
A dashboard says ninety percent complete.

7
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.968
Your task is to decide what the evidence
supports,

8
00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:26.764
not to maximize the completion percentage.

9
00:00:27.514 --> 00:00:30.138
A percentage can be useful for scheduling,

10
00:00:30.288 --> 00:00:34.192
but it treats unlike activities as if they
were interchangeable.

11
00:00:34.342 --> 00:00:38.928
Finishing several minor tasks does not
offset an unresolved requirement

12
00:00:39.078 --> 00:00:40.828
that affects product quality.

13
00:00:40.978 --> 00:00:45.074
The visual compares a large completion bar
with three named gaps.

14
00:00:45.224 --> 00:00:49.618
Read the gaps directly: mixing range,
cleaning evidence and alarm

15
00:00:49.768 --> 00:00:50.852
response.

16
00:00:51.002 --> 00:00:55.845
Their significance must be evaluated
individually in the context of the

17
00:00:55.995 --> 00:00:57.147
intended use.

18
00:00:57.897 --> 00:01:01.950
For this exercise, routine-use readiness
is not demonstrated.

19
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.449
State that conclusion, identify the
missing evidence,

20
00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:09.866
assign owners and define what must be
reviewed before a new decision.

21
00:01:10.016 --> 00:01:13.728
If a project proposes progression to a
limited next stage,

22
00:01:13.878 --> 00:01:18.230
assess that specific activity and its
dependencies separately through the

23
00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.596
approved system.

24
00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:23.821
Do not describe conditional progression as
general permission for

25
00:01:23.971 --> 00:01:25.058
production.

26
00:01:25.208 --> 00:01:28.579
The scope of an authorization must be
unambiguous.

27
00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:33.297
Complete the workbook and final
assessment, then compare your capstone

28
00:01:33.447 --> 00:01:34.855
with the model reasoning.

29
00:01:35.005 --> 00:01:38.780
You should now be able to explain the
purpose of the programme plan,

30
00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:43.303
draft testable requirements, connect them
to evidence and discuss risk

31
00:01:43.453 --> 00:01:45.266
without hiding behind scores.

32
00:01:45.416 --> 00:01:50.430
These self-study results are not a formal
qualification or competency

33
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:51.657
record.

34
00:01:51.807 --> 00:01:55.839
Apply the method with qualified
colleagues, current requirements and

35
00:01:55.989 --> 00:01:59.595
approved site procedures when working on a
real project.
